Improve Python reference resolution and uncertainty model

- Scope-stack resolution: bind function params and assignment targets as
  locals, so shadowing doesn't fabricate false usage edges.
- Import aliasing: import x as y and from x import y as z bind the alias
  and keep the target reachable.
- References carry resolved SymbolIds (not names), fixing alias/dynamic targets.
- Uncertain constructs marked: star imports (Dynamic), getattr (Reflection),
  __import__ (Dynamic); these downgrade to Probable, never Guaranteed bloat.
- 6 integration tests covering shadowing, aliasing, star imports, getattr,
  __import__, and cross-file usage.
